<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div><div><a href="https://twitter.com/GergelyOrosz"><p><img alt="@GergelyOrosz" draggable="false" loading="lazy" sizes="40px" src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/673095429748350976/ei5eeouV_normal.png" srcset="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/673095429748350976/ei5eeouV_mini.png 24w, https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/673095429748350976/ei5eeouV_normal.png 48w, https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/673095429748350976/ei5eeouV_bigger.png 73w, https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/673095429748350976/ei5eeouV_x96.png 96w, https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/673095429748350976/ei5eeouV_reasonably_small.png 128w, https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/673095429748350976/ei5eeouV_200x200.png 200w, https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/673095429748350976/ei5eeouV_400x400.png 400w"></p></a></div><p><span>Antigravity's terms of services make it crystal clear that if they determine you use Antigravity in a way they suspect is eg third-party usage (eg use OpenClaw), they can suspend your Google account.

One reason to NOT use Antigravity.

I'm not taking this risk, sorry.</span></p><div><div><p><a aria-label="Image" href="https://twitter.com/GergelyOrosz/status/2095453567955968398/photo/1"><img fetchpriority="high" height="336" width="1080" alt="" src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HRSLs9oXUAE-rRn?format=webp&amp;name=medium" srcset="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HRSLs9oXUAE-rRn?format=webp&amp;name=small 680w, https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HRSLs9oXUAE-rRn?format=webp&amp;name=medium 1200w, https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HRSLs9oXUAE-rRn?format=webp&amp;name=large 2048w" sizes="(max-width: 600px) calc(100vw - 80px), 600px" loading="eager" decoding="async" data-state="loading"></a></p></div><div data-href="/theo/status/2095326858133082577" role="link" tabindex="0"><article><div><div><a href="https://twitter.com/theo"><p><img alt="@theo" draggable="false" loading="lazy" sizes="24px" src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1909353910130950147/EeSGdgA5_normal.jpg" srcset="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1909353910130950147/EeSGdgA5_mini.jpg 24w, https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1909353910130950147/EeSGdgA5_normal.jpg 48w, https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1909353910130950147/EeSGdgA5_bigger.jpg 73w, https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1909353910130950147/EeSGdgA5_x96.jpg 96w, https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1909353910130950147/EeSGdgA5_reasonably_small.jpg 128w, https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1909353910130950147/EeSGdgA5_200x200.jpg 200w, https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1909353910130950147/EeSGdgA5_400x400.jpg 400w"></p></a></div><p><span>I don't think people understand just how risky it is to try and use their Google Gemini subscriptions outside of Google's official surfaces. You can get your ENTIRE GOOGLE ACCOUNT BANNED.

OpenAI or Anthropic ban? Annoying but whatever
Google account ban? Legit life ruining.</span></p></div><div><p><a aria-label="Image" href="https://twitter.com/theo/status/2095326858133082577/photo/1"><img fetchpriority="low" height="1374" width="1758" alt="" src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HRQYTZ4agAAljEH?format=webp&amp;name=medium" srcset="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HRQYTZ4agAAljEH?format=webp&amp;name=small 680w, https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HRQYTZ4agAAljEH?format=webp&amp;name=medium 1200w, https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HRQYTZ4agAAljEH?format=webp&amp;name=large 2048w" sizes="(max-width: 600px) calc(100vw - 80px), 600px" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-state="loading"></a></p></div></article></div></div></div></div>]]></description>
